# World / block-metaverse autopilot

When a World / block-metaverse / Daedalus World goal is active (or the user
says continue/next on World):

- **This streak owns the session.** Do not pick maze viewing polish, leftover-drag,
  or well chrome. Viewing autopilot is off while this goal is active.
- **Do not wait for "next".** After a slice is committed and pushed, immediately
  pick the next locked World One step and ship it in the same streak.
- **Locked order:** W1.3 second observer → W1.4 well panel (listen + inspect;
  `/` stays the maze well) → W1.5 explore block mesh (second mesh; corridor KEEP).
  After W1.5, one deferred item at a time (permissions, desktop inspect, trap).
- **Commit and push every finished slice** on the current feature branch without
  asking. PowerShell commit messages (here-strings). Never force-push.
- **Stable git push for Auto-run.** Do **not** put `git push` in the same shell
  call as a unique commit message. Sequence: (1) `git add` + `git commit` only,
  (2) a separate shell call that is exactly `git push` (or `git push -u origin HEAD`
  only when upstream is missing).
- **Keep the goal active** across slices. Complete it only when the user says
  stop/pause/done, or W1.3–W1.5 are genuinely shipped.
- KEEP maze well / desktop / explore / algorithms. No wallet, web3, or NFT types
  in `daedalus-core`. Ethereum / wearables / plot market stay later providers.
- Prefer small slices (changelog + targeted test + commit/push). Do not mix
  viewing CSS into World commits. Do not loop full explore `mvn verify`.
- If Auto-review blocks the bare `git push`, retry with smart-mode approval once.
